    "question": {
      ":question/id": "18455f84-dbba-5fbd-82d4-234bac4acd70",
      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[5]{x^{6}}}-2x^{3}-\\frac{3}{x^{6}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[5]{x^{6}}}-2x^{3}-\\frac{3}{x^{6}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(4x^{\\frac{-6}{5}}-2x^{3}-3x^{-6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 4\\int x^{\\frac{-6}{5}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-2\\int x^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-3\\int x^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 4\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-6}{5}+1}}{(\\frac{-6}{5}+1)}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{x^{3+1}}{(3+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad -3\\left(\\frac{x^{-6+1}}{(-6+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{20}{\\sqrt[5]{x}}-\\frac{x^{4}}{2}+\\frac{3}{5x^{5}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
