      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$-\\frac{2}{x^{6}}-2\\sqrt[7]{x}+x^{6}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-\\frac{2}{x^{6}}-2\\sqrt[7]{x}+x^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-2x^{-6}-2x^{\\frac{1}{7}}+x^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -2\\int x^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-2\\int x^{\\frac{1}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -2\\left(\\frac{x^{-6+1}}{(-6+1)}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{1}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{1}{7}+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +\\left(\\frac{x^{6+1}}{(6+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{2}{5x^{5}}-\\frac{7\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}{4}+\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
