      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}+x^{5}+\\sqrt[7]{x^{5}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}+x^{5}+\\sqrt[7]{x^{5}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-x^{-2}+x^{5}+x^{\\frac{5}{7}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{\\frac{5}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -\\left(\\frac{x^{-2+1}}{(-2+1)}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{x^{5+1}}{(5+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{5}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{5}{7}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x^{6}}{6}+\\frac{7\\sqrt[7]{x^{12}}}{12}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
