      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$\\frac{3}{x^{6}}+5x-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(\\frac{3}{x^{6}}+5x-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(3x^{-6}+5x-5x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 3\\int x^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+5\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x-5\\int x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 3\\left(\\frac{x^{-6+1}}{(-6+1)}\\right)+5\\left(\\frac{x^{1+1}}{(1+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad -5\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-8}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{-8}{7}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{3}{5x^{5}}+\\frac{5x^{2}}{2}+\\frac{35}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
